##### Step 5: Define Adapter Interface

Create domain-specific interface representing business capability abstracted from third-party API implementation details.

**Example: Drug Database Adapter Interface** (`IPharmacyDataProvider.cs`):

```csharp
namespace Gainwell.Pharmacy.Contracts;

/// <summary>
/// Provides pharmacy reference data and drug interaction checking.
/// Abstracts underlying drug database vendor (FDB, Medi-Span, etc.).
/// </summary>
public interface IPharmacyDataProvider
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Checks for drug-drug interactions between multiple medications.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="drugCodes">NDC drug codes to analyze for interactions</param>
    /// <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token</param>
    /// <returns>List of interactions with severity and clinical significance</returns>
    Task<DrugInteractionResult> GetDrugInteractionsAsync(
        IEnumerable<string> drugCodes,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);

    /// <summary>
    /// Retrieves pricing benchmark for drug based on AWP/WAC/MAC pricing.
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="drugCode">NDC drug code</param>
    /// <param name="quantity">Quantity dispensed</param>
    /// <param name="cancellationToken">Cancellation token</param>
    /// <returns>Pricing information including AWP, WAC, MAC</returns>
    Task<DrugPricingResult> GetDrugPricingAsync(
        string drugCode,
        decimal quantity,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default);
}

/// <summary>
/// Domain model for drug interaction results (Gainwell-specific, vendor-agnostic).
/// </summary>
public record DrugInteractionResult(
    IReadOnlyList<DrugInteraction> Interactions,
    DateTime RetrievedAt);

public record DrugInteraction(
    string InteractionId,
    string Drug1Code,
    string Drug1Name,
    string Drug2Code,
    string Drug2Name,
    InteractionSeverity Severity,
    string ClinicalSignificance,
    string ManagementRecommendation);

public enum InteractionSeverity
{
    Minor,
    Moderate,
    Major,
    Contraindicated
}
```

