#### Scenario 4: Drug Database Integration with Webhook Cache Invalidation

**Business Requirement**: First Databank publishes drug database updates monthly (new drugs, interaction changes, pricing updates) requiring Gainwell to invalidate cached drug data ensuring accurate clinical decisions.

**Challenge**: 15-minute cache TTL provides performance benefits (87% cache hit rate) but risks stale data if FDB publishes critical drug interaction change between cache refreshes.

**Solution: Webhook Cache Invalidation**:

```csharp
// FDB webhook endpoint receiving database update notifications
[HttpPost("/webhooks/fdb/database-updates")]
public async Task<IActionResult> HandleFdbDatabaseUpdate([FromBody] FdbWebhookPayload payload)
{
    _logger.LogInformation("Received FDB database update webhook: {UpdateType}", payload.UpdateType);

    if (payload.UpdateType == "DRUG_INTERACTIONS")
    {
        // Invalidate all cached drug interaction results
        var affectedDrugCodes = payload.AffectedDrugCodes;
        foreach (var drugCode in affectedDrugCodes)
        {
            var cachePattern = $"fdb_interactions_*{drugCode}*";
            await _cache.RemovePatternAsync(cachePattern);

            _logger.LogInformation(
                "Invalidated FDB interaction cache for drug {DrugCode}",
                drugCode);
        }

        // Emit metric tracking cache invalidations
        _cacheInvalidationCounter.WithLabels("fdb", "drug_interactions").Inc(affectedDrugCodes.Count);
    }
    else if (payload.UpdateType == "DRUG_PRICING")
    {
        // Invalidate pricing cache for affected drugs
        var affectedDrugCodes = payload.AffectedDrugCodes;
        foreach (var drugCode in affectedDrugCodes)
        {
            var cacheKey = $"fdb_pricing_{drugCode}";
            await _cache.RemoveAsync(cacheKey);
        }
    }

    return Ok();
}
```

**Benefits**:
- **Real-Time Data Accuracy**: Critical drug interaction changes invalidate cache immediately upon FDB publication vs waiting up to 15 minutes for TTL expiration
- **Maintained Cache Performance**: Selective invalidation preserves 87% cache hit rate for non-affected drugs vs full cache flush requiring all requests to call FDB API
- **Audit Trail**: Webhook processing logs provide compliance evidence that Gainwell systems reflect latest drug database updates supporting state contract requirements
